Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: original Stardew Valley medicinal CROP GROWTH SPRITESHEET. One square transparent sprite atlas. STRICT regular EIGHT COLUMNS by FOUR ROWS. Logical canvas 128x128 pixels. Each cell is 16 logical pixels wide by 32 logical pixels tall, giving exactly 8x4 cells. All plants centered horizontally, roots on the SAME BASELINE at 2 logical pixels above bottom of each cell. No roots below baseline. Up to 14 logical pixels wide and 23 tall. No ground patches, no soil tiles, no pots.
The FOUR ROWS are four distinct fictional herbs, always in this order:
row1 GLASS DEWBERRY: a compact teal-leaved shrub, mature stage bears THREE OVERSIZED ROUND SKY-BLUE GLASS-MARBLE BERRIES, dark cobalt crescent shadows, bold square ivory upper-left glints, cyan reflected edges. These big berries are the focus. Leaves small and dark teal.
row2 MOONVELVET: sage green round leaves with pale silvery edges, TWO or THREE big rounded drooping pale-lavender bellflowers with plum centers. Not lavender spikes.
row3 AMBER HEARTLEAF: low branching reddish stems with round HEART-SHAPED AMBER-GOLD LEAVES and dark red-brown veins, tiny orange resin droplet. No flowers or berries.
row4 SILVER SEAMLEAF: upright fan of narrow pointed SILVERY MINT LEAVES, pale stitch-like midribs and one tiny ivory blossom.
Every row has the EXACT SAME eight stages left to right:
column0 a tiny brown split seed at baseline (2x2 logical pixels);
column1 a tiny two-leaf green sprout (3x4 pixels), near baseline;
column2 a small distinct juvenile plant with four leaves (7x8 pixels);
column3 a larger preharvest plant with buds or folded leaves, characteristic colors becoming visible (10x15 pixels);
column4 the FULL MATURE HARVESTABLE PLANT with lush characteristic flowers/berries/leaves (14x22 pixels);
column5 the JUST-HARVESTED REGROWTH plant, SAME full-size stems and low leaves as column4 but no berries, flowers removed and/or amber/silver harvest leaves clipped, clear empty stems (12x15 pixels);
column6 another FULL MATURE PLANT matching column4, same size (14x22 pixels);
column7 dried wilted brown version, same baseline (10x15 pixels).
Authentic vanilla Stardew Valley farm-crop PIXEL ART. Imagine drawing on the actual 128x128 low-resolution logical grid and enlarging with nearest-neighbor: big crisp uniformly square pixels, one-logical-pixel dark warm outlines, clean stepped curves, 3-4 hue-shifted tones per material, cozy saturated colors, bright upper-left highlights. Every growth stage must remain simple and readable at 16x32. All cells cleanly separated, transparent gaps, identical scale.
Real alpha transparency. No background, no painted checkerboard, no drawn grid, no text, no labels, no pots, no ground shadows, no floating decorations, no smooth gradients, no antialiasing, no realism. Exactly 32 crop-stage sprites on a mathematically regular 8-column 4-row grid.
